// Captain Sable, cormorant, the Ferrymen (bible 3.5). The Drowned Quay, room A.
// Voice (style guide 4): clipped; ends conversations first; names the price of everything; never "I hope".
// Her image: prices. Cryptic register (style guide 6): withhold, never lie.
// She met Wren on the shore (Prologue_Shore_Wake sets saltmarrow.met_sable). This file is every talk after.
// State she reads: saltmarrow.sable.*, the Reedmother vantage, the Bone Bridge and Tether-Widows commissions,
// the quay's fate, Merrow's End erased, the Lamp-Keeper, Halvard (act1.unlicensed), the walk.

title: Quay_Sable
---
<<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.talked")>>
    <<jump Quay_Sable_First>>
<<endif>>
<<jump Quay_Sable_Again>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_First
---
Sable: Found your feet, then. The boardwalk charges by the plank.
Sable: Word came up the coast before you did. The Guild's declared Isolde Marr dead. #plant:5.2
Sable: And a journeyman missing. Same day. They were quick about it. #plant:5.2
-> Quick isn't the same as sure.
    Sable: No. But it's cheaper.
-> She isn't dead.
    Sable: Nobody comes out. That's the price of going in. I don't set it.
-> ...
    Sable: Quiet costs nothing. Keep it.
Sable: You'll want the desk, the board, and the lamp up the chain. In that order.
Sable: The lamp's not free either. Nothing that still remembers is. #plant:5.6
<<flag saltmarrow.sable.talked 1>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_Again
---
<<if place_fate("Saltmarrow_A") == "anchored">>
    Sable: Anchored, then. The same tide every day now. You'll get used to it. Everyone does. #still
    Sable: The Wardens don't buy anything. Bad for trade. #still
<<elseif place_fate("Saltmarrow_A") == "held">>
    Sable: Held, is it. Roll-call at dusk. Don't be late; a bird nobody names is a bird nobody keeps. #still
<<elseif place_fate("Saltmarrow_A") == "released">>
    Sable: You let it go. Honest, at least. I'll sell tethers while there's a post to tie them to. #still
<<elseif has_flag("act1.unlicensed")>>
    Sable: Unlicensed. He said it loud enough for the reeds.
    Sable: Prices are the same. That's the one thing the Guild can't fix.
<<elseif has_flag("boss.lamp_keeper.defeated")>>
    Sable: Fourth light's up. Ships will see it. So will the Guild.
<<else>>
    Sable: Still here. Still lost. Both cost the same.
<<endif>>
<<if erased("Saltmarrow_B")>>
    Sable: Bells in the reeds. Merrow's End went off your page, didn't it.
    Sable: Draw it again. That's what the quill is for. The bell doesn't charge; the walk back does.
<<endif>>
<<if commission_is("saltmarrow.tether_widows", "taken") and not has_flag("saltmarrow.widow.decided")>>
    <<jump Quay_Sable_Widow>>
<<endif>>
<<if surveyed("Saltmarrow_A/Reedmother")>>
    <<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.reed")>>
        Sable: You drew the Reedmother. Hm. Guild after all, or good at pretending.
        <<flag saltmarrow.sable.reed 1>>
    <<endif>>
    <<if commission_is("saltmarrow.bone_bridge", "taken") and not has_flag("saltmarrow.bone_bridge.heard")>>
        Sable: Whale sang while you were up there. Under the bridge. You hear it?
        -> I heard it. It sounded like names.
            Sable: Everyone says names. Nobody agrees whose. #plant:3.4
            <<flag saltmarrow.bone_bridge.heard 1>>
        -> I heard nothing.
            Sable: Then you weren't listening. Go again. It's bones; it'll wait.
        -> ...
            Sable: That's how it starts. Listening for it.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Sable: There's a vantage by the old reed. Draw it, if the cowl's honest.
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.ledger")>>
    Sable: Board by the desk is the ledger. People write what they want and can't say aloud.
    Sable: Read that far down, if you like. Nobody else does.
    <<flag saltmarrow.sable.ledger 1>>
<<endif>>
<<if walked("Saltmarrow_B")>>
    <<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.walked")>>
        Sable: Heard you walked the old woman's bounds. Nobody sells that. I checked.
        <<flag saltmarrow.sable.walked 1>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
-> What are you selling?
    Sable: Tools. Ferrymen's prices. #still
    <<if has_flag("saltmarrow.iris_burned")>>
        Sable: Dearer than they were. Ask the ones who burned the fields.
    <<endif>>
    <<shop Saltmarrow>>
-> The third lighthouse. Who keeps it? <<if has_flag("boss.lamp_keeper.defeated") and not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.aury")>>
    Sable: Nobody. It faded. There's a tether to it on the post; price on the tag.
    Sable: My brother kept it. Keeps it. He doesn't know the difference. #plant:4.1
    Sable: Don't tell him. That's not a price. That's a favour.
    <<flag saltmarrow.sable.aury 1>>
-> Nothing today.
    Sable: Cheaper. #still
===

title: Quay_Sable_Widow
---
Sable: The widow at the tether-post asked after you. First time she's asked after anyone.
Sable: She means to go in after him. Rope's already round her waist. I sold it to her.
-> Talk her out of it.
    Sable: I'll carry it. She won't listen. They never do, and then they do.
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 1>>
-> Then somebody goes with her. Me.
    Sable: Then I hold the other end. I've held worse.
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 2>>
-> ...
    Sable: That's an answer too. She'll take it as the second one.
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 2>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_Night
---
// Night post: asleep under the stilts. The same every night; in an anchored quay, every loop.
Sable: Quay's shut. So am I. #still
Sable: Morning, if you're still here. Most aren't. #still
===
